WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:08.510
A gig on Game of Thrones is a proven career
enhancer. But the show's actors didn't materialize

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:13.450
out of thin air. Most of them had careers
prior to finding their way to the Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.619
And not everything they worked on was what
you'd consider HBO-level material. For your

00:00:18.619 --> 00:00:24.950
amusement (and their chagrin), here are early
roles of Thrones cast members during the "pre-Game"

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.140
era...

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.960
Emilia Clarke

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.320
Before she was an international superstar
as Daenerys Targaryen, Emilia Clarke had virtually

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.930
no on-camera experience as an actress. She'd
been on one episode of the UK show, Doctors,

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:45.579
and one SyFy Original Movie. Fortunately,
that movie—Triassic Attack from 2010—provided

00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:49.970
her with the opportunity to say, "Why, yes,
I do have experience working with giant reptilian

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:54.270
beasts." And that takes you surprisingly far
in the world of Game of Thrones.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.370
Lena Headey

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:02.149
Ironically, Cersei Lannister actress Lena
Headey's first performance for American television

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:06.329
was in the last outing of Richard Dean Anderson
as the one and only...MacGyver.

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:10.720
(MacGyver music playing)

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:16.460
In this TV movie from 1994, Headey plays Elise
Moran, whose father is killed. That sets a

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.280
series of spine-tingling events into motion,
which find MacGyver doing what he does best:

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.549
saving the day when the odds are against him.
Headey's character survives, and ends up on-screen

00:01:26.549 --> 00:01:31.400
at the very end. That means she has the honor
of being the last person to share a conversation

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:37.460
with MacGyver. Why, that's almost as impressive
as being Queen of Westeros...

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.590
Alfie Allen

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:44.159
When the opportunity arises to take the spotlight,
there's only one thing to do: take it and

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:48.759
run. That's what Alfie Allen—better known
as Theon Greyjoy—does in the 2004 sequel

00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:50.460
to Agent Cody Banks.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.770
In the scene, the student orchestra playing
in front of Queen Elizabeth and visiting heads

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:58.460
of state has to kill time to prevent the G7
Summit meeting from starting. When the call

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:04.490
goes out to improvise, Allen is challenged
to "go for it." So he struts over to the microphone,

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:10.830
slips on a headband, and launches into a German-accented
version of Edwin Starr's "War." See for yourself:

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:19.370
(singing)

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.720
Conleth Hill

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.390
If you thought playing a character whose main
character trait includes a lack of private

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:31.830
parts was emasculating, you should talk to
actor Conleth Hill. He plays Varys the Spider

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:37.000
on Game of Thrones. And in 2008, the veteran
actor also played an old, bed-ridden lady

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.410
in the British reality show spoof, Britain's
got the Pop Factor...and Possibly a New Celebrity

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:46.319
Jesus Christ Soapstar Superstar Strictly on
Ice.

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:49.349
Yes, that's the actual title.

00:02:49.349 --> 00:02:51.860
Jonathan Pryce

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:56.360
Character actor Jonathan Pryce has been working
for so many years that it almost seems unfair

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:01.920
to dig through his catalog in search of something
embarrassing. Instead, let's spotlight a project

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.160
relatively few Americans know about: his turn
as the Master.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.050
That's right, we mean the long-lived Doctor
Who villain, but it's not an incarnation you

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:13.510
would've seen battling Doctors Nine, Ten,
Eleven, or Twelve.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:20.129
No, Pryce found himself doing battle against…Rowan
"Mr. Bean" Atkinson? Yes, in a very special

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:25.110
Doctor Who serial made for Comic Relief, Atkinson
played the Doctor and went toe-to-toe with

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:29.550
Pryce before he hung up his weird jacket and
became the High Sparrow we love to hate on

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:30.739
Game of Thrones.

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:36.620
And yes, we know all about Shae and her grown-up
film career before being cast on Game of Thrones.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.500
You'll have to leave YouTube to learn more
about that one...

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:43.060
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:47.120
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which early role of these Game of

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.920
Thrones actors surprised you the most.

